{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>ואליו הוא נושא</b> etc. <b>והיה בך חטא.</b> The intention is that although oppressing the wage of a hired worker is nothing other than stealing money, nevertheless its punishment is not monetary but capital — and this is what the verse says: ״יִהְיֶה בְךָ״, meaning ״in you״ — in your soul; ״חֵטְא״ — in the manner of (1 Kings 1:21) ״וְהָיִיתִי אֲנִי וּבְנִי שְׁלֹמֹה חַטָּאִים״. And it prefaced the reason for the punishment by saying ״וְאֵלָיו הוּא נוֹשֵׂא אֶת נַפְשׁוֹ״ — and hence the justice will be a soul for a soul."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:51.816508794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}